[box=My favourite Touhou characters :)]
I've played hundreds of hours of Touhou 6, to the point where it hits me pretty hard emotionally-wise. That's why Reimu is my favourite character not only from Touhou, but from anywhere, and by far: one-tricking a character in a videogame you love simply changes your way of being. You can feel you are ONE with the character. It moves as you want it to move. It's like a 6th sense. A part of your body, even. So I believe it's only natural that I eventually got fond of Reimu this much, mostly by Touhou 6 alone.

My second favourite character is Remilia. She's always looking for new adventures to spend her immortality with and never gets bored, and I feel somewhat relatable in this regard - I always say that if I had a hundred lives, I'd do a hundred different things with them. There's just so many books to read, so many videogames to play, so much music to listen to, so many sports, professions, hobbies, people to meet and love!

All this being said, it's not like I personally feel like any character "represents me" as a person - they're just that for me, characters. Simple drawings and concepts. I'm a real, flesh person. I feel characters as a way to further evoke or understand my feelings, not as something I would 100% relate to (no "she's me, fr fr!" feeling for me "^^)
